<section class="opening" aria-labelledby="constructs-title">
  <h1 id="constructs-title">Constructs</h1>
  <p class="lede">The shapes a line of Spw takes, one card each: what it reads as, what holds it, what it holds, and how often the 1119 lines on the shelf use it. Every name on a card is a door to that card.</p>
  <figure class="anatomy" aria-labelledby="anatomy-title">
  <figcaption id="anatomy-title">One line from spwashi.com's home page, taken apart. Each part opens its card.</figcaption>
  <p class="anatomy-line"><code><a class="seg" href="#c-word">home</a><a class="seg" href="#c-mode"><span data-t="b-mode">[</span>hook<span data-t="b-mode">]</span></a><a class="seg" href="#c-definition"><span data-t="b-direction">{</span>software.art.practice<span data-t="b-direction">}</span></a><a class="seg" href="#c-scene"><span data-t="b-scene">(</span>atlas<span data-t="b-scene">)</span></a><a class="seg" href="#c-concept"><span data-t="b-concept">&lt;</span>person<span data-t="b-concept">&gt;</span></a></code></p>
  <ol class="anatomy-keys"><li><a href="#c-word"><code>home</code></a> the word</li><li><a href="#c-mode"><code>[hook]</code></a> the lens</li><li><a href="#c-definition"><code>{software.art.practice}</code></a> what it holds</li><li><a href="#c-scene"><code>(atlas)</code></a> the scene</li><li><a href="#c-concept"><code>&lt;person&gt;</code></a> where it goes</li></ol>
</figure>
